# Radio

- One Tokio task owns each companion. Bluetooth allows one client. The phone app must be disconnected.
- Connecting over Bluetooth asks for the six-digit companion PIN, pairs through the system agent, then opens the GATT session. Do not show the PIN in the message list or status text after entry.
- On connect: app start, device query, set the clock, incremental `get_contacts(since)`, drain queued messages, subscribe, auto-fetch.
- Persist every parsed contact and message field, plus a JSON snapshot. Do not drop unknown values.
- Save latitude and longitude only when an advert or telemetry includes them. Ignore 0,0.
- Always store hop count. Resolve a route from `CMD_GET_ADVERT_PATH` (`0x2A`), then the contact outbound path, then a path-update event. An operator trace is separate and costs airtime.
- Match hop hashes to known keys. Two matches is ambiguous. Do not guess.
- The radio contact table is finite (`max_contacts`). Do not auto-add every public advert onto the radio.
- Reconnect with backoff unless the operator disconnected. Dedupe messages by sender, timestamp, and text.
- Mesh text is at most 160 bytes.
